From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:45:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: preallocate flight and job bookkeeping to
 fixed bounds

run_job, the job worker and retirement are in the fence-signalling path,
yet they grew vectors with GFP_KERNEL: run_job allocated each job's
history and pushed it into the inbox, admission and take_finished grew
the engine's lists every pass, reserve_flight grew the flight,
publication and ledger vectors, and each retire scan reserved its list.

Every one of these has a fixed bound:
- at most JOB_CREDITS (128) jobs are between run_job and their fence,
  since the device scheduler's credit limit is that constant and each job
  takes one credit, so the inbox, the engine's job list and a reusable
  finished list are preallocated to it; admission drains the inbox in
  place, keeping its capacity;
- MAX_FLIGHTS (1024) Works may be in flight, above the logged churn peak
  of under 400: flights, retirements, publications, the ledger and the
  issued list are preallocated to it at init, and reserve_flight returns
  EBUSY at the cap (backpressure admission already retries) instead of
  growing them;
- a job's history (64 commands at most, plus the previous stamp) is
  allocated by SUBMIT and carried in the scheduler job.

About 1 MiB in total. Work arena refills, scratch leases, alias page
tables and TVB growth still allocate; see the phase-2 design note.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
